`src/aedist/plot_cost_quality.py`).

## A. Coverage, not accuracy (author question — confirmed)

Ground truth: the Y axis IS coverage, not accuracy. `plot_cost_quality.py`
ylabel is "Assets correctly identified" (`:174`), docstring "Y axis:
per-model count of correctly identified plants (true positives)" (`:16`).
So any "accuracy"/"quality" wording in the figure TITLE/suptitle (check
`plot_cost_quality.py:176` `fig.suptitle(...)`) is wrong — it should say
**coverage**.
- Fix the suptitle (and ylabel if it should read "Coverage (assets
  correctly identified)") so the figure is labelled coverage, not
  accuracy/quality. Regenerate `fig_direct_cost_quality.pdf` via the
  `make`/`render.mk` target; commit the regenerated PDF.

## B. Replace the caption (author's words)

Current caption (`:618–630`) is long and carries filenames
(`\texttt{modelset\_exp1\_batch2}`, `\texttt{…cost\_quality.csv}`) — both
violate the standalone-caption policy [[0606]]. Replace the WHOLE caption
with:

> Coverage (Y) vs. cost (log-scale X), Experiment 1. Prices and models as
> of May 2026. More expensive models discover more assets and return more
> stable results. Source: author; see \ref{sec:annex-exp1}.

Notes:
- "[REF EXPERIMENT 1 ANNEX]" → `\ref{sec:annex-exp1}` (no hardcoded annex
  letter; house rule).
- No filenames in the caption (the CSV/modelset detail lives in the
  annex).
- Grammar: "returns" → "return" (subject "models" is plural).
- Em dashes literal "—" (U+2014) if any.
- Keep the dashed reference line / panel content as-is in the figure; this
  is a caption + label change, not a data change.

